Transitive dependencies with attribution requirements
-----------------------------------------------------

The Rust crate dependency graph was audited with `cargo deny check
licenses` (see `deny.toml` for the allow-list). All transitive
dependencies use permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
BSD-3-Clause, ISC, MPL-2.0, NCSA, Unicode-3.0, Zlib, CC0-1.0). Per-
dependency copyright notices live inside each crate's own
`LICENSE`/`COPYING` file as distributed on crates.io; this NOTICE
intentionally does NOT replicate them — consult the upstream crate
metadata for authoritative attribution.

Notable groups:

- `unicode-*` crates (unicode-bidi, unicode-ident, unicode-linebreak,
  unicode-segmentation, unicode-width) — dual MIT/Apache-2.0, with
  upstream Unicode data covered by the Unicode-3.0 license.
- `wgpu`, `winit`, `objc2-*`, `windows-*` family — permissive
  MIT/Apache-2.0 or Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.

